module System

### Any crashable: the error a `check` caught, whatever its type. `is Crashables e` on a `Check`
### binds it. It holds the crashable itself, in a room the program's largest crashable fits in, with the crashable's
### type id in front, so `crash_title`, `crash_message`, `represent` and `diagnose` reach that crashable's own: the
### builder chooses the routine by the type id, among the crashables the program throws. While a failure passes up
### through the routines it fails, the crashable sits in the failure mold of the flow it was thrown on (each thread and
### each coroutine has one) and the room is empty: the `check` that receives it copies it into the room. The carrier
### that caught the error holds what the crashable holds (a `Text` field), and a `Crashables` read out of it is valid
### while the carrier holds the error.
record Crashables
    ### The type id of the crashable it holds.
    secret type_id: U64
    ### The number of the failure, which says where it was first thrown (0 when the build keeps no trace). Its top bit
    ### is set while the crashable is still in the flow's mold.
    secret failure: U64
    ### The crashable itself, once a `check` kept it: the builder sizes this room for the program's largest crashable
    ### (64 bytes at the least).
    secret data: Array[U64, 8]

### The caught error's title: its type's name in sentence case, unless the crashable writes its own.
### :returns: The title.
@readonly
@innate
routine Crashables.crash_title() -> Text

### The caught error's message.
### :returns: The message.
@readonly
@innate
routine Crashables.crash_message() -> Text

### The caught error as text: its message.
### :returns: The message.
@readonly
@override
@innate
routine Crashables.represent() -> Text

### The caught error for diagnostics: its type, message and member variables.
### :returns: The diagnostic text.
@readonly
@override
@innate
routine Crashables.diagnose() -> Text

### The caught error's type id, the one a type pattern on a carrier compares.
### :returns: The type id.
@readonly
@innate
routine Crashables.crash_type_id() -> U64

### Gives back what the caught error holds (its `Text` fields). Only the carrier that owns the error calls this.
@innate
dangerous routine Crashables.free()

### The first of the 32 frames of the trace the error was first thrown with, a ring its depth indexes modulo 32, or
### null when the thread no longer remembers it (made on another thread, or later failures took its place).
### :returns: The address of frame 0.
@untraced
dangerous routine Crashables.thrown_trace_frames() -> Hijacked[TraceFrame]
    return LLVM::failure_trace_frames(seq: me.failure & (U64_MAX >>> 1))

### How many frames the trace had when the error was first thrown (0 when the build keeps no trace, or the thread no
### longer remembers it).
### :returns: The depth.
@untraced
dangerous routine Crashables.thrown_trace_depth() -> S32
    return LLVM::failure_trace_depth(seq: me.failure & (U64_MAX >>> 1))
